TEST: does M-in-gap FORCE a long sub-AP? Sample N=7 families, bin by M, report longest-AP len.
  =2/15       : n=   22  longest-AP len: min=4 max=6 mean=4.55  (N-2=5)
  loose>2/15  : n=39901  longest-AP len: min=2 max=7 mean=3.41  (N-2=5)

If IN-GAP families reliably have longest-AP >= N-2 (while loose ones are smaller), that is the
FREIMAN SIGNATURE: gap => (N-2)-AP + 2 defects => reduces to the 2-outlier ladder (fleet-swept
empty at N=12). The Freiman-stability step 'M in gap => (N-2)-sub-AP' is then THE crux to prove.
